15161 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 15162 0 R/Alt(Block diagram. At the top, the 8-bit data_i enters the D input of the storage block mem_q, whose four entries 0 to 3 feed a 4:1 multiplexer that drives the 8-bit data_o. Below it on the left, push_i and the inverted full_o enter an AND gate, whose output push drives the EN input of the register wr_ptr_q[2:0] and the EN input of the storage. On the right, pop_i and the inverted empty_o enter an AND gate, whose output pop drives the EN input of the register rd_ptr_q[2:0]. Each pointer register returns its 3-bit Q output through a +1 block to its D input and has the inputs clk_i and rst_ni. Bits 1 and 0 of wr_ptr_q drive the address A of the storage, and bits 1 and 0 of rd_ptr_q drive the select of the multiplexer. At the bottom, the comparator on the right compares both 3-bit pointers and drives empty_o. The comparator on the left compares the 3-bit wr_ptr_q with bits 1 and 0 of rd_ptr_q and with bit 2 of rd_ptr_q, the wrap bit, which passes an inverter first, and drives full_o. Both flags also return to the inverted inputs of the AND gates.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 31635 0 R>>
endobj
